{"request_id":"sha256:88f4da572577025de7b1beb16a02d31cf446b84dc1e4f46006bea1ee2fa72d57","units":[{"unit_id":"sha256:b310efaf23ffc795abfa6e1ffd47d0b90d24cdea5182ce7ab1036ff0e9320e8c","reviewed":true,"findings":[{"kind":"AVAILABLE_CAPACITY","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":809}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. states that its in-house manufacturing facility and its partnership with Flex maintained a combined manufacturing capacity of approximately five-million microinverters per quarter, reflecting the domestic manufacturing footprint as of the 2025 fiscal year. This is a current available manufacturing capacity figure for microinverters, expressed in units per quarter."},{"kind":"CAPACITY_QUALITATIVE","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":834}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. states that it outsources some of its manufacturing to third-party contract manufacturers and believes its contract manufacturing partners have sufficient production capacity to meet anticipated demand for its products for the foreseeable future. This is a qualitative statement about contract manufacturing production capacity for the registrant's products, without a comparable actual-output/capacity pair."},{"kind":"SALES_OR_SHIPMENTS","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":883}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports that during the year ended December 31, 2025 it sold approximately 6.4 million microinverter units and shipped 706.1 MWh of IQ Batteries, compared to approximately 6.5 million microinverter units and 521 MWh of IQ Batteries shipped in the year ended December 31, 2024. These are sales/shipment quantities, not actual production."},{"kind":"SALES_OR_SHIPMENTS","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":804}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. states that as of December 31, 2025 it has shipped approximately 86.4 million microinverters and that more than 5.1 million Enphase residential and commercial systems have been deployed in over 160 countries. These are cumulative shipment/deployment figures, not actual production."},{"kind":"SALES_OR_SHIPMENTS","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":884}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports $91.2 million of microinverter shipments associated with safe harbor transactions with customers in the year ended December 31, 2025. This is a shipment amount, not actual production."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":806}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. describes fiscal year 2025 priorities including scaling U.S. manufacturing and advancing product qualification for the Section 48E investment tax credit and the AMPTC under Section 45X. This is a strategic/contextual statement about manufacturing priorities, not a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":818}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. states it has relocated a significant portion of its manufacturing to the United States while continuing to utilize contract manufacturing in China and India, and that certain critical components are still sourced from outside the United States. This is a contextual statement about manufacturing location and sourcing, not a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":819}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. states that LFP battery cells used in its energy storage systems are still supplied exclusively by two vendors located in China and that identifying qualified alternative suppliers with the necessary expertise and capacity remains challenging. This is a supply-chain contextual statement about supplier capacity, not the registrant's manufacturing capacity or production."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":986}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports open purchase obligations of $252.3 million related to component inventory that it and its primary contract manufacturers procure on its behalf in accordance with its production forecast. This is a purchase commitment amount, not a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":737}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. lists a manufacturing facility and warehouse facility in Arlington, U.S. with approximately 227,344 square feet leased through January 2031. This is a property/real-estate disclosure, not a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":830}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. describes cost of revenues components including product costs, warranty, manufacturing and installation services, and states that AMPTC earned under the IRA for U.S. manufactured microinverters shipped to customers are treated as a reduction to cost of revenues. This is an accounting/contextual statement, not a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":899}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports AMPTC benefits recognized of $238.7 million for the year ended December 31, 2025, compared to $157.5 million for the same period in 2024, related to U.S. manufactured microinverters and IQ Batteries MWh shipped to customers. This is a tax credit benefit amount, not a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":900}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports a 16.2 percentage point AMPTC benefit in gross margin for the year ended December 31, 2025, compared to an 11.8 percentage point benefit in 2024, due to a higher proportion of sales from U.S. manufactured microinverters and IQ Battery MWh shipped. This is a margin/tax credit contextual statement, not a production or capacity quantity."}],"unresolved":[],"calculation_limits":["TARGET_CURRENT_PRODUCTION_NOT_PRESENT_IN_THIS_UNIT","QUANTITIES_NOT_COMPARABLE"]}]}